 "result": "**Where to look**\n- `src/tessel/sessions.py:304-312`: the session serializer builds its key list from `SECRET_KEY` plus `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY`. Signing uses the current key, and verification tries each key in the list.\n- `src/tessel/app.py:210-211`: the config defaults (`SECRET_KEY`, `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY`, both `None`).\n- `docs/config.rst:114-141`: the docs for rotation.\n\nYou were most likely logged out because the old key wasn't kept in `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY`, so existing session cookies failed signature verification.\n\n**How to rotate without logging anyone out**\n1. Put the new key in `SECRET_KEY` and move the old one into `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY`:\n   ```python\n   SECRET_KEY = \"new-key\"\n   SECRET_KEY_HISTORY = [\"old-key\"]\n   ```\n2. Old cookies still verify, and they get re-signed with the new key when the session is next saved.\n3. After your session lifetime has passed (`PERMANENT_SESSION_LIFETIME`), remove the old key from the history.\n\n**Caveats**\n- `docs/config.rst:141` notes that extensions using `SECRET_KEY` directly (e.g. for CSRF tokens or other signed data) may not support the history list yet. Check any you use.\n- `CHANGES.rst:61` references a security advisory tied to this setting. Skim it to confirm which version you're on has the fix.",
